    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 107</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_107/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 23:42:46 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_107/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the correct output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#xA;    i := 1&#xA;    s := []string{&amp;#34;A&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;B&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;C&amp;#34;}&#xA;    i, s[i-1] = 2, &amp;#34;Z&amp;#34;&#xA;    fmt.Printf(&amp;#34;s: %v \n&amp;#34;, s)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;A. s: [Z,B,C]&#xA;B. s: [A,Z,C]&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Parallel assignment: &lt;code&gt;a[i], a[j] = a[j], a[i]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Multiple assignment is divided into two steps, with a specific order:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Evaluate the index expressions and address expressions on the left side of the equals sign, and then evaluate the expressions on the right side of the equals sign.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Assignment.&#xA;Therefore, in this example, &lt;code&gt;s[i-1]&lt;/code&gt; is calculated first. Since the two expressions on the right side of the equals sign are constants, the assignment operation is equivalent to &lt;code&gt;i, s[0] = 2, &amp;quot;Z&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;/details&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description>
    </item>
